/* --- the DS4's Bluetooth confirmation tones, pre-encoded ------------------
 *
 * GENERATED by tools/ds4-tone-gen in the listener repo, and NOT hand edited.
 * Unlike the DualSense's table next door, the tool that made this one IS
 * committed, so these bytes are reproducible rather than merely described.
 * ASCII only on purpose: a generated file is regenerated, not read.
 *
 * THE FORMAT IS THE MAP'S, NOT A CHOICE MADE HERE.
 * maps/ds4_usb_over_ds4_bt.map, LAYOUT B: 32000 Hz, joint stereo, loudness,
 * bitpool 48, 16 blocks, 8 subbands -> 109 bytes per frame, 128 samples,
 * 4 ms. A 0x14 report carries TWO of these. Those numbers are what the pad
 * is already fed by the host every time a game plays a sound, so they are
 * proven rather than derived.
 *
 * THREE TONES, and the order they play in is the message:
 *   handing over   low  then high   -- rising, going to the host
 *   handed back    high then low    -- falling, coming home
 *   refused        low  then LOWER  -- sinking, it did not happen
 * The same
 * vocabulary the DualSense uses, at the same two frequencies, so one pad
 * does not mean something different from the other.
 *
 * The envelope HOLDS rather than fades, and the low note is lifted -- both
 * learned by ear on the DualSense and carried over rather than
 * rediscovered. See ctm_bt_signal_data.inl. */

